{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa98294201430b3fb01e4f629eb02dbea8afbc9975da9332f632e6daccf0757d","digest":{"component_or_area":"store read surfaces (show/list/search/ready)","key_entities":["ensure_fresh","_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT","src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5(tracker)>","_clear_sync_throttle","REBAR_SYNC_PUSH","tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py","tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py","--output json"],"problem_keywords":["read-output integrity","concurrent writes","sync contention","stalling reads","reconverge lock","empty stdout","JSON parsing"],"propositions":["Every CLI read surface (show, list, search, ready) must output parseable JSON or exit nonzero when invoked under concurrent write-burst contention with background pushes, never silent empty stdout with exit 0.","The reconverge lock throttle marker must be cleared before each parameterized read invocation to ensure every surface exercises the reconverge path rather than short-circuiting to the local snapshot.","Exit 0 with valid-empty JSON (e.g. []) is acceptable; exit 0 with truncated or malformed stdout is a bug.","The property test harness reuses the ed2b generator (repo_with_origin_tickets, _rebar_cli, _clear_sync_throttle) rather than duplicating per-surface test logic.","Reads stalling on the held writer lock beyond a timeout threshold (e.g. >10s) constitute a regression in the lock-wait bound."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787725885925428001,"uuid":"29e1a621-88dc-450c-8d97-f51c248e7586"}